messages:
samir: FYI I'm opening a refresh PR for the Quickstart (HelloMini). Goals: migrate snippets to SDK v4, add a tiny TypeScript quickstart, tidy the auth section for short-lived tokens, and add a single-file Docker deploy example. WIP: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4188. Need reviewers on TS snippets + the deploy guide.

miriam: Nicely scoped. Two quick asks: 1) keep the Node example under ~20 lines so its copy-pastable; 2) call out ‘do not embed tokens in frontend bundles’ with a one-liner about proxying requests.

jonah: CI flagged the TS examples: eslint/ts errors when run with our CI image. We either pin typescript/eslint or adjust the tsconfig. Quick workaround in the PR: add a minimal tsconfig.json to the example folder so the smoke script can compile.

tina: Also suggest adding a streaming example (server->client) since a lot of users expect streaming in quickstarts. Tiny snippet for fetch + abort signal: 
```
// browser streaming example (minimal)
const res = await fetch('/api/generate', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }) });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let done = false;
while (!done) {
  const { value, done: d } = await reader.read();
  if (value) console.log(decoder.decode(value));
  done = d;
}
```
Include a short note: "Use abort controller to cancel long streams."

docs-bot: link-checker: broken link detected -> /guides/deploy/docker (404). Reported and added as comment on PR.

samir: Thanks. I'll update the deploy link to `/guides/deploy/containerize` and replace the Compose example with a single-file Dockerfile + run note. Also will shorten the Node snippet to be copy-pasteable per @miriam.

miriam: One more content weed: in the migration section, add a tiny snippet mapping v3->v4 usage. E.g. `const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY })` vs old `createClient(...)`. Keep it one code block.

jonah: CI run (pre-merge) failing on the auth rotation test: our smoke harness sets REDWOOD_API_KEY but some examples check REDWOOD_TOKEN. Can we standardize in the quickstart and add a fallback in the example README? Something like: `export REDWOOD_API_KEY=${REDWOOD_API_KEY:-$REDWOOD_TOKEN}`. I'll push that to CI config in the PR.

tina: A11y check: the token copy button needs an aria-label and keyboard focus instructions. I can draft the small note and ping @samir for placement. Also recommend adding `role=\"status\"` on the inline-copy confirmation toast for screen readers.

samir: Great — please add that text as a tiny subsection under "Getting your API key" and mark it as optional. Ill also add the README fallback line and the changed Dockerfile.

ci-bot: CI: smoke run queued for PR #4188. Current status: lint -> passing, unit -> passing, e2e -> failing (auth rotation test). Logs: "token rotated: expected header REDWOOD-KEY, got none".

jonah: Pushed a quickfix to the example harness to export both env vars; re-triggering CI.

miriam: When the CI passes, I can do a short copy edit pass (tone + keep-language simple) and merge. Please tag me in the PR comments.

tina: If we merge, make a follow-up issue to audit all quickstarts for streaming examples and a11y. Small ticket so we don't block this merge.

samir: Plan: finish edits tonight, trigger final smoke run, aim to merge Friday morning if green. Tagging reviewers: @miriam (copy edit), @tina (a11y), @jonah (CI/harness). Thanks everyone :rocket:
